plan Package
title   Package routes, dependency identity, declarations and installed consumers
status  proposed
goal
    One ESM package whose supported imports, declarations and host boundaries agree with the
    capability plans. This plan owns what a consumer can import and how installed use is proven;
    runtime behaviour stays with its owners.
outcomes
    O1  Routes
        Exactly six routes exist, through explicit package exports and ESM import conditions; no
        CommonJS, wildcard subpath or deep import is supported. Each exposes only these names:

        - flow-state: definition, machine, trait, subroutine, app, `actorRef`, `runtimeSetup`,
          resource, transaction, stream, Feed, deny, check, send, FlowError, Flow (with Flow.Guard,
          Flow.Callback, Flow.Exit, Flow.optional, Flow.uncertain, Flow.annotate, Flow.input,
          Flow.initial, Flow.private, Flow.Denial, Flow.ignore, Flow.state, Flow.entry, the Flow.is*
          predicates and the Flow.Payload and Flow.Filling types), Outcome (Outcome.success,
          Outcome.failure, Outcome.unknown), entity, domain, read, write, listen, and the condition
          operators eq, `oneOf`, contains, between, overlaps, gt, gte, lt, lte, `isNull`, and, or,
          not, `serverMatches`, asc, desc; types Definition, Machine, App, ActorRef, Actor,
          Snapshot, Runtime, RuntimeSetup, Diagnostic and Attempt. Attempt is also a Schema value
          carrying id and encoded input (@plan.Operations.O3). The setup's services Layer is typed
          by the machines' R, read from the contracts' services lists (@plan.Runtime.O2).
        - flow-state/react: FlowProvider, `useActorByRef`, `useActor`, `useView`, `useNow`, Hydrate.
        - flow-state/testing: Story, Fake (with Fake.server, Fake.storage and the answer classes
          Fake.Lost, Fake.Refused and Fake.Closed), `propertyTest`, `domainPropertyOptions`,
          `defineConfig`, StoryFrame, StoryPlayer, `definePresentation`, the error class
          PropertyTestFailed; types StoryRun. There is no test-runner adapter package (proposed).
        - flow-state/inspect: inspect, render, `attachInspector`, trace (an object with only import
          and export); types Model and Trace.
        - flow-state/server: dehydrate; type Hydration.
        - flow-state/persistence: layerIndexedDb({ database? }).

        Every other setting or operation is a member of these values, inferred data or an Effect
        primitive. No route re-exports another route's names or internal services, stores,
        ManagedRuntime or mutable harnesses. flow-state/internal/testing, which exports
        disposeRuntime for Flow's own suite, is not a supported route and is not one of the six.

        flow-state/react keeps the "use client" directive in its emitted JavaScript; a Next.js
        Server Component may import its components, and hooks run only on the client.
        flow-state/server resolves to the real module under react-server and node conditions and to
        a stub under browser and default, browser winning over a conflicting node condition.

        The stub throws FlowError ServerOnlyImport on evaluation, before any work; it never supplies
        server execution. A non-Node server host selects react-server.

        The root imports no React, server-only or Node code, testing, inspection tooling, TypeScript
        compiler, renderer or IndexedDB, so it runs in request runtimes and edge hosts.

        Every route except react imports without React installed; only rendering StoryFrame or
        StoryPlayer needs React, so a no-React project can load its Story config. Importing the
        persistence route outside a browser is safe; storage access begins only when its Layer is
        acquired (@plan.Persistence.O1).
    O2  Dependencies and inert imports
        Effect is a peer dependency, never bundled, so Runtime, Schema, Context tags and Layers
        resolve to the consumer's single Effect instance. The published peer range is exactly 4.0.5
        until packed-consumer proofs cover a wider range. KeyValueStore comes from
        effect/persistence. React is an optional peer, majors 18 and 19; a host without React fails
        only where it uses the React route, StoryFrame or StoryPlayer.

        package.json declares sideEffects: false. Importing any route constructs no Runtime,
        registers no listener and performs no storage I/O, actor work or user callback. Tree shaking
        never makes a used server-only import succeed in a client bundle.
    O3  Types and removed surfaces
        Packed declarations preserve literal inference, nominal machine and definition identity,
        exact unions and field presence, variance, service requirements and failure channels.
        Consumers need no any, assertions, explicit generic arguments or wrappers.

        Lanes are inferred _tag unions; RuntimeSetup is inferred from the returned setup.
        Declarations are self-contained: no workspace path, internal route or unresolved import
        escapes, and consumers emit isolated declarations without excessive instantiation.

        Removed surfaces are gone, with no alias, overload, adapter or deprecated wrapper. They are
        those in the "Deleted or absorbed" table of references/design/minimal-library.md, plus
        registered views, child and dynamic actors, leases, final/onDone/output, `useShallow` and
        custom comparators, `useResource`, callable Stories and mutable harnesses, saved behaviour
        artifacts, compression, Implementation values and the separate error classes
        (FlowUsageError, FlowPersistenceError, FlowDisposeError, FlowStoryExecutionError), model and
        story (the testing route's old Story constructor).

        PropertyTestFailed, which carries a property test's result, is the testing route's one error
        class.

        A configuration object naming a removed or unknown field throws InvalidConfiguration with
        its path and help naming the replacement, before any work starts.
    O4  Installed consumers
        Dispatch Desk is a checked-in application compiled and run against the packed tarball, never
        workspace aliases; it and the seven entity examples become real consumers at S10. Its
        Next.js App Router host proves request render, Hydrate first render without mismatch, reload
        restore, reconnect, disposal, scope isolation and a second tab running without persistence.

        Chromium, Gecko and WebKit, at the versions the pinned harness supplies, run its React
        lifetimes, real IndexedDB, reloads and hydration.

        Small and medium consumers compile with strict checking, isolatedModules and isolated
        declarations, and packed execution proves each route, including no-React and React 18 and 19
        installs. Every build stage gate runs these packed-consumer checks. The installed flow
        binary resolves the same package identity as the consumer (@plan.CommandLine.O6).
decisions
    D1  Six closed routes
        The root keeps the authoring surface; React, server, testing, inspection and storage are
        isolated so a consumer pays only for what it imports.
    D2  Owners define semantics; this plan proves installed reachability
        Package checks preserve owner types and behaviour across publishing and host boundaries;
        they never replace owner proofs.
constraints
    C1  Portable bytes
        Identity, key and structural codecs use ECMAScript and Web APIs (TextEncoder), never Node
        Buffer or UTF-16 counts. Equal accepted data gives equal bytes on Node, Bun, Deno, Chromium,
        Gecko and WebKit; limits belong to @plan.Inspection.O2.
    C2  Generated output
        dist, declarations and docs come from pinned build scripts, never hand edits.
verification
    V1  Packed exports and declarations match the six lists exactly; deep imports, cross-route
        re-exports and every removed name fail; strict isolated consumers compile.
    V2  A no-React consumer imports every route except react; React 18 and 19 hosts run; one Effect
        identity is shared; "use client" survives bundling; browser bundles reach ServerOnlyImport;
        import spies see no work.
    V3  Codec vectors give equal bytes on every listed host; removed configuration fields throw
        InvalidConfiguration before any side effect.
    V4  Packed Dispatch Desk passes its Next.js, isolation, reload, uncertainty and second-tab gates
        in Chromium, Gecko and WebKit.
